Room: the external protocol request of a Room page goes to the host.

Chrome confirms a link to another application (mailto:, a custom scheme)
in a Views tab-modal dialog (ExternalProtocolDialog over its BrowserView). A
Room page's request belongs to the host's confirmation (the Engine
protocol's shouldOpenExternalProtocol, Phase 3.4b: confirmed once per
scheme). Chrome's checks before the dialog stay (the block state and
policy, the handler's existence, Room not being the handler); "open" is
Chrome's LaunchUrlWithoutSecurityCheck, as the dialog's OK.

No existing hook: RunExternalProtocolDialog is a static defined once per UI
toolkit (this file on desktop) and called by external_protocol_handler.cc;
the only override, ExternalProtocolHandler::SetDelegateForTesting, replaces
the whole handler (block state, the shell worker, the launch) and is
test-only. //room takes the request only for pages it wraps whose delegate
answers it; every other page keeps Chrome's dialog.

Phase 3.4b, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_page_dialogs.mm.
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/external_protocol_dialog.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/external_protocol_dialog.cc
